Multichannel LPCM output path for ao_avfoundation (Pippin-original, no upstream).

On Apple / AVFoundation, only Dolby formats (AC-3 / E-AC-3 / MAT-Atmos) can be
bitstreamed by a third-party app; Pippin's 0006 handles those on the compressed
passthrough path. DTS, DTS-HD MA, TrueHD and multichannel FLAC/PCM CANNOT be
bitstream-passed-through by a third-party app on Apple platforms, so parity comes
from a robust multichannel LPCM path: once mpv has decoded such sources to PCM,
emit correctly-laid-out 5.1 / 7.1 (or a clean stereo downmix) to the renderer.

This patch reworks ONLY the non-compressed (PCM) branch of ao_avfoundation.m and
leaves Pippin's 0006 AC-3 / E-AC-3 passthrough untouched. It:

  1. Channel layout + order. For a recognized 5.1 / 7.1 bed it rewrites
     ao->channels into a canonical CoreAudio MPEG order and describes the format
     with the matching standard layout TAG, instead of a bag of per-channel
     descriptions the HDMI/AVFoundation path has to guess from. mpv reorders its
     decoded output to ao->channels and the layout is built from that same order,
     so data and layout are consistent by construction:

       mpv speaker order                         CoreAudio tag / slot order
       ----------------------------------------  ---------------------------------
       5.1  FL FR FC LFE (BL|SL) (BR|SR)          MPEG_5_1_A  L R C LFE Ls Rs
       7.1  FL FR FC LFE  SL SR  BL BR            MPEG_7_1_C  L R C LFE Ls Rs Rls Rrs

     For 7.1 mpv's SIDE pair (SL/SR) maps to the tag's primary surround (Ls/Rs)
     and mpv's BACK pair (BL/BR) to the rear surround (Rls/Rrs), matching a
     physical home-theatre 7.1 bed. Any other configuration (mono, stereo,
     3.0/4.0, 6.1, exotic 8ch, height beds) is left on mpv's existing
     description-based layout (ca_get_acl) unchanged.

  2. Route capability negotiation (tvOS/iOS). Before locking the format, the
     output route is checked with the same positive-evidence rule the compressed
     path uses: supportedOutputChannelLayouts is populated for CarPlay/AirPlay
     and empty by design on HDMI, so a non-empty list with no >2ch entry is the
     only "stereo only" signal; empty/unavailable stays "unknown" and never
     blocks multichannel. When the route is stereo-only, ao->channels is dropped
     to stereo so the CORE downmixes cleanly rather than shipping 5.1/7.1 the
     system would silently fold or drop. Route-change and rendering-capabilities
     notifications are observed and, edge-triggered, request a reload when the
     stereo/multichannel boundary is crossed (mirrors edde746 libmpv 0010's
     spdif route-capability observation, adapted to the PCM path).

  3. Conservative fallback. Anything uncertain falls back to the exact stock PCM
     behavior; the compressed AC-3 / E-AC-3 path from Pippin's 0006 is untouched.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (same as mpv). Applies after Pippin's libmpv 0006.
